  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. The rule hasn't run yet (its status is \"pending\"), so I haven't seen it evaluate. I also couldn't check its filter against the real data: `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` is empty in my shell, which blocked direct queries to Elasticsearch.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` uses `timestamp` as its time field. Each document is one web request:\n- **Request details:** client IP (`clientip`), URL (`url`, `request`), file extension (`extension`), HTTP status (`response`), size in bytes (`bytes`) and browser (`agent`).\n- **Location:** source and destination country (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`) and coordinates (`geo.coordinates`).\n- **Client machine:** operating system and RAM (`machine.os`, `machine.ram`).\n- **Other fields:** `host`, `referer`, `tags` and memory figures.\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-7430cd87 Web logs overview\"** has 7 panels and shows the last 7 days by default:\n- Single numbers for total requests, unique visitors (distinct client IPs) and total bytes served.\n- Requests over time, split by response code (top 5).\n- A pie chart of each response code's share.\n- A table of the top 10 URLs, with request count and bytes.\n- Requests by source country (top 10).\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-7430cd87-web-logs-overview-eae8f7ef9b09\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-7430cd87 5xx spike\"** (id `1b5fb220-19dd-4d77-ac77-c3c11218c8f5`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`:\n- It checks every minute.\n- It counts requests whose `response.keyword` starts with \"5\" (any 5xx code) over the last 5 minutes and fires when the count is more than 10.\n\nThe \"starts with 5\" filter assumes response codes are stored as text like \"503\" in `response.keyword`. That is how Kibana's sample data normally stores them, but I couldn't confirm it here.\n\nThe rule has no actions attached, so a firing alert only appears in Kibana and doesn't notify anyone. Tell me if you want one added, for example Slack or email.",
